## Approach

- Keep the refactor mechanical.
- Move code blocks without changing literals, argv shape, side effects, or print order.
- Prefer one-call-site helpers over new abstractions.
- Pin orchestration order explicitly; extraction must not move the feature-description gate before reset, codex sidecars inside the launch guard, or dirty-tree detection before dispatch selection.
- Pin inline-fallback helper output order to the live monolithic block; treat the numbered sequence in `_handle_step2b_drafter_inline_fallback` as normative for wrapper-visible stdout.
- Pin `_read_step2b_drafter_result` to structure inspection only; defer `diff_lines` to the success handler immediately before the ✅ print.
- Pin every action emission through `_emit_drafter_next_action`; the delimiter is part of the wrapper contract.
- Pin `_shared_step2b_postplan_body` invocation args and per-rc stdout/action ordering in the success handler.
- Keep silent subprocess redirection on scout `append-entry` and inline-fallback `append-failure`.
- Keep `step2b_drafter_main` readable enough that future changes do not re-grow complexity.
- Run baseline regeneration only after code complexity is back under the approved caps.

## Edge cases

- `DESIGN_TMPDIR` missing, invalid, or relative.
- Folded Step 2a sentinel prep failure.
- Pause requested before drafter launch.
- Pause requested during postplan rc11.
- Invalid Claude model with whitespace.
- Git status failure while capturing baseline (must unlink stale porcelain).
- `feature-description.txt` missing or empty after artifact reset (rc `1`, no action).
- Dirty sidecar present with `STATUS=dirty` and `MODE=baseline-delta`.
- Dirty sidecar absent but baseline porcelain differs.
- Drafter writes a plan without `PLAN_WRITTEN=true`.
- Drafter succeeds structurally but scout manifest is missing or invalid (stderr warning + silent append-entry).
- Codex vendor with `skip_reason` set: no launch, `drafter_rc == 2`, sidecars still appended.
- Postplan rc10 schedules inline retry only when the current logic says so (depends on conditional `.step2b-postplan-fallback-used` seed).
- Dialectic candidate promotion failure warns but does not fail the run.
- Handler return codes must not be dropped by a thin main (no double emission).
- Inline fallback with `skip_reason` set or nonzero `drafter_rc`: warning and action rows still emit before fallback log and run-log append.
- `diff_lines` must not be parsed on dirty or inline-fallback paths.
- Raw `DRAFTER_NEXT_ACTION=` prints break rc11 pause gating and wrapper row parsing.

## Failure modes

- Helper extraction can reorder stdout or stderr. Preserve the current order; inline-fallback is especially sensitive (warning and action rows before file writes).
- Helper extraction can move a side effect across the dirty-tree check or feature-description gate. Do not do that.
- Folding codex sidecars into the launch helper drops ledger updates on skip paths.
- Unconditional `true` for `.step2b-postplan-fallback-used` breaks rc10 inline-retry scheduling.
- Leaving baseline porcelain after git-status failure can misroute dirty-tree recovery.
- Regenerating the baseline before the refactor can lock in bad metrics. Regenerate only after refactoring.
- New helpers can become new complexity offenders. Keep them small.
- Thin main that ignores handler `int` returns can fall through and double-emit `DRAFTER_NEXT_ACTION`.
- Inline-fallback helper that lists file writes before warning/`DRAFTER_VENDOR`/action emission drops the warning or reorders wrapper-parseable stdout.
- Parsing `diff_lines` in `_read_step2b_drafter_result` can change branch assumptions or success logging on non-success paths.
- Bare action prints omit `STEP2B_DRAFTER_WRAPPER_ROWS_BEGIN=1` and break tests plus wrapper routing.
- Dropping `DEVNULL` on run-log subprocesses can leak KV lines after trusted action rows.
- Wrong `site` or missing `defer_pause_save=True` on postplan can break rc11 pause ownership or drift-baseline seeding.

